  lbOpen: 'See the build step by step', dlgClose: 'Close',
  extHint: (mod, bp) => `Rather not build it by hand? The ${mod} mod splits equally among its outputs with no splitter tree, and ${bp} has ready-made balancer blueprints shared by other players.`,
  extBp: 'blueprints on Satisfactory Calculator',
  whyVsTitle: 'Balancer or another alternative?',
  whyIsBest: 'The balancer is the recommended alternative here: it fills every destination with fewer pieces than the others.',
  whyVsBest: (title, full, po, pb) => `The recommended one, “${title}”, ${full ? 'also fills every destination' : 'doesn’t fill every destination'} with ${po} pieces in the middle. This balancer uses ${pb}.`,
  whyBalWhen: 'A balancer pays off when you want every destination line at the same rate, or when you’ll change the machines later and don’t want to rewire.',
  whyOverflow: 'Overflow (Smart Splitter) only passes on what’s left of a line that already filled its own destination. It’s cheap, but it doesn’t even out the lines.',
  stepBal: (ins, n, m, name, per) => `Middle: ${ins} go into a ${n}→${m} balancer (${name}). Each destination gets up to ${per}/min; the piece-by-piece build is under “See the build step by step”.`,
