  bpFits: mk => `fits the Blueprint Designer Mk${mk}`, bpNone: 'bigger than the Blueprint Designer Mk3 (6×6): build it straight on the ground or in parts',
  tipSpace: 'Measured on the plan: only the splitters, mergers and the belts between them; the input and output belts come in from the edge. Blueprint Designer Mk1 is 4×4 foundations (32 m), Mk2 5×5 (40 m), Mk3 6×6 (48 m). The plan is one roomy way to build it; in the game you can squeeze it.',
  planNote: 'Top view, to scale: the grid is 8 m foundations, each piece takes ¼ of a foundation (4×4 m) and two connected pieces always have a piece of belt between them. The arrow on a piece shows its front output.',
  hint2dMarks: 'Ctrl + drag moves a Blueprint Designer marker.',
  bpMarksAria: 'Blueprint Designer markers', bpMarkAdd: mk => `+ Mk${mk}`,
  bpMarkAddAria: (mk, f) => `Add a Blueprint Designer Mk${mk} marker (${f}×${f} foundations)`,
  bpMove: 'Move marker', bpMarkName: (n, mk, f) => `#${n} · Mk${mk} ${f}×${f}`, bpMarkRemove: name => `Remove marker ${name}`,
  bpMarksNone: 'no markers', lgDesigner: 'Blueprint Designer (marker)',
  tipBpMarks: 'Add markers the size of the Blueprint Designers (Mk1 4×4, Mk2 5×5, Mk3 6×6 foundations) to plan how many blueprints to build the balancer in. Ctrl + drag (Cmd on Mac) on a marker moves only that marker, one metre at a time, so you can place it however you like; dragging without Ctrl moves the view. On a phone, turn on Move marker and drag. If the balancer fits a designer, the smallest one that fits already shows covering it. Markers don’t check the pieces, they are only for you to slice it up. They belong to this build: changing N→M, rate, tier or build style resets them.',
